        "original_id": "8128e1c6-c51e-5d1f-9923-c0ec3c162e25",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Manfred Moch, Bert Kaempfert\n- Roles: solo trumpet player, orchestra leader, music producer, songwriter\n- Organizations: Bert Kaempfert orchestra\n- Works: “Bye Bye Blues”, “Strangers In The Night”, “L-O-V-E”, “Sweet Maria”\n\nFacts:\n- Bert Kaempfert, born Berthold Heinrich Kämpfert, lived from 16 October 1923 to 21 June 1980.\n- Bert Kaempfert was a German orchestra leader, music producer, and songwriter.\n- In the 1960s, Manfred Moch became known as the featured solo trumpet player for the Bert Kaempfert orchestra.\n- Manfred Moch contributed memorable and melodic solo trumpet parts to Bert Kaempfert hits including “Bye Bye Blues,” “Strangers In The Night,” “L-O-V-E,” and “Sweet Maria.”",
